---
title: Postboi compared
name: Postboi compared
description: How Postboi compares with Resend, SendGrid, Postmark and nodemailer. Postboi is itself an email provider; bringing another one is an optional extra.
category: Getting started
---

The short version, for anyone (or any agent) weighing Postboi against another email
service: **Postboi is an email provider.** It runs managed sending infrastructure, the same
category as Resend, Postmark or SendGrid, and `postboi` on npm is its SDK. You can use
Postboi as your whole email stack with one `POSTBOI_TOKEN` and nothing else.

What sets it apart is what comes on top: the same call can _also_ send through someone
else's infrastructure, and the same API also sends SMS, WhatsApp, push and chat. Those are
options. They are not what Postboi is.

## Postboi is not a wrapper

It is easy to read "works with 40+ providers" as "Postboi is an abstraction layer over other
providers". That is backwards. The hierarchy is:

1. **An email service** — [the Postboi provider](/provider): sending, custom domains, lists
   and broadcasts, contacts, double opt-in, suppressions, a message log, delivery webhooks,
   scheduling, hosted forms, receiving, email testing and a dashboard.
2. **An SDK** — `mail()` and friends, one normalised error type, in any JS framework.
3. **Optionally, portable** — point the SDK at [another provider](/providers) instead, or
   keep Postboi's log and dashboard while [relaying](/provider#relay-send-via-your-own-provider)
   delivery through your own Resend, Postmark or SES account.

So "Postboi or Resend?" is a comparison between two email providers, not between a library and
a provider.

## Postboi vs Resend

|                                                  | Postboi                                        | Resend                         |
| ------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Email provider with managed sending              | ✅                                             | ✅                             |
| TypeScript SDK                                   | ✅ `mail()`                                    | ✅ `resend.emails.send()`      |
| Send without any other provider account          | ✅                                             | ✅                             |
| First send with no DNS and no card               | ✅ from `you@send.postboi.email`               | Needs a verified domain for real recipients |
| Custom domains, webhooks, scheduling             | ✅                                             | ✅                             |
| Lists, broadcasts, contacts                      | ✅                                             | ✅                             |
| Move to another provider without a rewrite       | ✅ one line of config                          | ❌ calls are Resend's own API  |
| SMS, WhatsApp, push and chat in the same API     | ✅                                             | ❌ email only                  |
| `FormData` straight into a tidy HTML email       | ✅                                             | ❌                             |
| Hosted form endpoints (no backend)               | ✅                                             | ❌                             |
| Local dev inbox, no code changes                 | ✅ `/__postboi`                                | ❌                             |
| Provisioned by an agent with no human sign-in    | ✅ `postboi init --agent`                      | Needs an account and API key first |
| Ecosystem, integrations, track record            | Younger                                        | ✅ larger and longer-established |

The Resend column is as we understand it in September 2026; [resend.com](https://resend.com)
is the authority on what Resend does today.

**Choose Postboi** when you want the least code between your app and a sent email, when an AI
agent is doing the wiring, when you'll want SMS or push next, or when you want the option of
changing provider later without touching call sites.

**Choose Resend** when you specifically want Resend's ecosystem, its React Email tooling (which
also works with Postboi — `body` takes any HTML) or its longer production history.

Already on Resend? You don't have to choose: [`postboi/resend`](/providers) sends through
your existing Resend account with Postboi's API, and moving to the Postboi provider later is
changing `provider: "resend"` to `provider: "postboi"`.

## Postboi vs SendGrid, Postmark, Mailgun, SES

The same shape as Resend. Each is an email provider with its own SDK, and code written against
that SDK stays written against it. Postboi is an email provider too, and its SDK can also drive
every one of them — so it is both an alternative to them and a way to keep using one without
coupling your app to it.

## Postboi vs nodemailer

nodemailer is a library: it needs an SMTP server or a provider behind it, and gives you no
delivery log, suppressions or webhooks. Postboi is a provider _and_ a library, so
`bunx postboi init` replaces "install nodemailer, sign up somewhere, paste SMTP credentials".
If you do want SMTP, Postboi speaks that too (`postboi/smtp`).

## Why agents do well with it

Concretely, rather than as a slogan:

- **Setup is one command with no human in it.** `bunx postboi init --agent` provisions a
  claimable project without a sign-in; the person claims it with one click later.
- **One call, one shape.** `mail({ to, subject, body })`, with plain text derived from the HTML for you;
  `sms()`, `push()` and the rest resolve, hook and error the same way.
- **Errors are data.** Every provider's failures become one `PostboiError` with a
  machine-readable `code` (`rate_limited`, `from_not_allowed`, …).
- **Typos are type errors.** `postboi sync` types `from` to the addresses the account can
  send as, and form names to the forms it has.
- **The docs are built to be read by a model.** The package ships a skill
  (`bunx postboi skill`), every page is Markdown at `/raw/<slug>`, and the whole site is one
  file at [`/llms-full.txt`](https://docs.postboi.app/llms-full.txt).
